1
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:25,000
Come on, Si. Help me out.

2
00:01:25,080 --> 00:01:28,040
-Please lend me a hundred grand.
-Ugh!

3
00:01:28,120 --> 00:01:31,920
I have no money for you.
Auem's still paying off Yod's debts.

4
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:33,720
But I really need it!

5
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:37,680
-I need this money to help Orn.
-Don't give her any!

6
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:40,960
Look.

7
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:42,640
Instead of working,

8
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:45,440
you're just going around
begging people for money?

9
00:01:45,520 --> 00:01:46,920
Well, I'm broke.

10
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:48,880
-Will you help me?
-No freaking way!

11
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:52,760
I told you to help me sell meatballs,
but you wouldn't.

12
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:54,520
Now you're asking for my money?

13
00:01:55,120 --> 00:01:58,000
If you're not helping me,
then stop nagging!

14
00:01:58,720 --> 00:02:02,360
Okay. Let me be perfectly clear here.

15
00:02:02,440 --> 00:02:04,560
If anyone here
lends their money to Sa-Ing,

16
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:06,240
go get your money from her.

17
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:08,639
Don't you go to Auem!

18
00:02:08,720 --> 00:02:10,639
Or so help me!

19
00:02:11,760 --> 00:02:14,400
You'd better take your wife back home.

20
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:16,120
How I get my money doesn't concern you.

21
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:18,720
No one cares about that,

22
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:21,040
but don't make it Auem's problem.

23
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:22,960
Think about your daughter.

24
00:02:23,480 --> 00:02:25,320
You only care about Auem.

25
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:27,720
What about Orn?

26
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:31,560
She's just a kid who made a mistake.
Shouldn't we just forgive her?

27
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:35,840
So? Will you please lend me some money?

28
00:02:35,920 --> 00:02:40,560
-Please? Just this once.
-Come pick your fresh prawns right here.

29
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:42,760
Okay.

30
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:47,000
Fresh prawns.

31
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:48,880
I'll try somewhere else.

32
00:02:53,280 --> 00:02:55,080
BOONYOD FARM

33
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:00,960
Yod.

34
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:03,000
Please put yourself in my shoes.

35
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:05,240
Orn's really in trouble,

36
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:08,200
so I had to pawn the gold you gave me

37
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:10,640
to help our child.

38
00:03:10,720 --> 00:03:13,160
BOONYOD THADAMIT

39
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:16,400
Please don't be mad at Orn.

40
00:03:16,920 --> 00:03:19,920
I'll get it back from the pawn shop
as soon as I have some money.

41
00:03:25,320 --> 00:03:27,240
What are you guys doing here?

42
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:32,720
You're home late again, Orn?

43
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:35,920
Where have you been? These past few days,
you've been coming home late.

44
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:39,280
I've been working
so I can pay off my debt.

45
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:40,880
What kind of work?

46
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:42,080
And where?

47
00:03:42,920 --> 00:03:45,160
It doesn't matter, Mom. I'm exhausted.

48
00:03:46,880 --> 00:03:47,880
Orn.

49
00:03:48,560 --> 00:03:49,840
You don't need to do that.

50
00:03:50,560 --> 00:03:53,200
I pawned my gold and got 100,000.

51
00:03:53,760 --> 00:03:55,880
That's not enough.

52
00:03:58,760 --> 00:04:00,160
I have to make the money myself

53
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:03,040
since none of my siblings
would want to help me.

54
00:04:45,520 --> 00:04:47,200
Auem, do you want to help Orn?

55
00:04:52,440 --> 00:04:53,920
What do you think Dad would do

56
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:56,400
if he was here?

57
00:04:58,200 --> 00:05:01,040
He was kind. He'd help Orn for sure.

58
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:05,920
But if I help her this time,

59
00:05:07,080 --> 00:05:09,040
wouldn't that make things
too easy for her?

60
00:05:10,560 --> 00:05:12,360
And if she causes trouble again,

61
00:05:12,440 --> 00:05:15,320
she might think that
someone's going to help her anyway.

62
00:05:15,400 --> 00:05:17,120
I think so too.

63
00:05:17,840 --> 00:05:18,920
But

64
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,720
Orn's our little sister.

65
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:23,080
We didn't abandon Hom Thong.

66
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:25,200
How could we abandon her?

67
00:05:28,440 --> 00:05:29,760
You mean,

68
00:05:31,440 --> 00:05:33,960
you'd be okay with me using our money

69
00:05:35,040 --> 00:05:36,040
to help Orn, right?

70
00:05:36,640 --> 00:05:37,720
Yeah.

71
00:05:38,280 --> 00:05:41,400
I believe that if we work together
and get more money,

72
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:43,000
we'll have enough just in time.

73
00:05:46,760 --> 00:05:48,120
We will.

74
00:05:49,200 --> 00:05:50,560
Yeah.

75
00:06:03,760 --> 00:06:05,440
Please order my lettuce next week.

76
00:06:05,520 --> 00:06:09,200
CASIO WATCH SOLD HERE

77
00:06:11,640 --> 00:06:13,120
Please wait here a sec.

78
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:26,120
Okay, let's go.

79
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:28,520
CLOTHING SECTION

80
00:06:28,600 --> 00:06:29,480
Huh?

81
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:49,200
Thank you.

82
00:07:10,920 --> 00:07:13,840
M BANK SAVINGS ACCOUNT

83
00:07:19,880 --> 00:07:21,000
Hello? Hi, Din.

84
00:07:21,680 --> 00:07:24,440
Hi, Auem. You said that Orn's now

85
00:07:25,240 --> 00:07:26,960
working part-time after school?

86
00:07:28,040 --> 00:07:29,800
Yes, why?

87
00:07:29,880 --> 00:07:31,720
She lied.

88
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:33,240
She skipped school to go to work.

89
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:36,480
And where is she now?

90
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:38,040
At a coffee shop.

91
00:07:38,120 --> 00:07:39,360
I'll get a video for you.

92
00:07:54,520 --> 00:07:57,960
-Here you go.
-Thank you.

93
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:12,560
Ugh.

94
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:17,080
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Hello.</font></font></i>

95
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:18,520
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Welcome.</font></font></i>

96
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:36,799
BOONYOD FARM

97
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:43,320
Oh, you're home.

98
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:46,000
Have you had dinner?

99
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:48,840
Mom made some stuffed omelets.
I'll heat them up for you.

100
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:51,920
What got into you?

101
00:08:55,120 --> 00:08:56,400
I'm worried about you.

102
00:09:03,680 --> 00:09:05,440
Didn't you scrape your knee this morning?

103
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:08,000
How did you know?

104
00:09:09,120 --> 00:09:10,600
Please go back to school.

105
00:09:11,280 --> 00:09:12,640
Don't skip school like this.

106
00:09:15,280 --> 00:09:16,120
Who told you?

107
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:18,080
Or were you spying on me?

108
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:20,600
You never trusted me, did you?

109
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:22,360
Why?

110
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:25,560
I bet you're worried
that I'll drag you into another mess.

111
00:09:26,520 --> 00:09:28,280
You're only nice to me

112
00:09:29,280 --> 00:09:31,320
so you can hold it over my head later.

113
00:09:31,400 --> 00:09:33,080
So you can order me around, right?

114
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:53,320
I'm sorry, Orn.

115
00:09:57,240 --> 00:09:58,960
I'm sorry I was such a bad sister

116
00:10:00,200 --> 00:10:01,720
that you didn't want to come to me.

117
00:10:10,560 --> 00:10:11,840
Now I know

118
00:10:14,560 --> 00:10:16,800
that some of the things you did

119
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:19,520
were because of me.

120
00:10:20,080 --> 00:10:21,720
I've been bossing you around

121
00:10:22,320 --> 00:10:24,160
and neglecting your feelings.

122
00:10:24,920 --> 00:10:26,120
You're our little sister.

123
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:29,080
We'll never turn our backs on you.

124
00:10:39,800 --> 00:10:41,240
I just want you to know

125
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:44,720
that I always want what's best for you.

126
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:48,840
But there are some things
I can't give you.

127
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:52,680
I may be able to help you today,

128
00:10:53,680 --> 00:10:55,440
but if this happens again…

129
00:11:02,200 --> 00:11:05,680
There won't be next time, I promise.

130
00:11:05,760 --> 00:11:06,960
I've learned my lesson.

131
00:12:00,440 --> 00:12:01,600
I'm sorry.

132
00:12:04,160 --> 00:12:05,120
I'm sorry.

133
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:09,040
I'm sorry.

134
00:12:11,160 --> 00:12:12,280
I'm sorry.

135
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:16,560
I'm sorry.

136
00:12:19,040 --> 00:12:21,000
-Bye.
-Bye.

137
00:12:22,040 --> 00:12:22,960
All done now.

138
00:12:23,560 --> 00:12:25,560
-Thank you so much.
-Thank you.

139
00:12:30,680 --> 00:12:32,760
Promise me you won't do this ever again.

140
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:33,800
Never again.

141
00:12:34,360 --> 00:12:35,400
Sure?

142
00:12:36,280 --> 00:12:37,360
Here, give me a hug.

143
00:12:39,280 --> 00:12:42,680
-And don't be so stubborn.
-I won't!

144
00:12:48,320 --> 00:12:49,760
Hom Ngern.

145
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:51,440
I'm sorry

146
00:12:52,040 --> 00:12:55,200
for using some of the Hom Thong fund
to pay off my debt.

147
00:12:56,880 --> 00:12:58,440
But I promise

148
00:12:59,040 --> 00:13:00,720
that I'll help earn some money

149
00:13:01,520 --> 00:13:04,160
and bring your son back to you.

150
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:16,240
Heard that, Hom Ngern?

151
00:13:19,120 --> 00:13:26,080
DO IT FOR HOM THONG

152
00:13:27,960 --> 00:13:30,120
This is all we've got in the bank.

153
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:31,040
With this money

154
00:13:31,120 --> 00:13:34,040
and the 100,000 Mom got
from pawning her gold to help us,

155
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:37,200
we just need to make 740,000 more
in the next three months.

156
00:13:37,280 --> 00:13:38,480
Come again?

157
00:13:38,560 --> 00:13:40,000
We need 740,000.

158
00:13:40,080 --> 00:13:42,200
Seven hundred and forty thousand
in three months?

159
00:13:44,720 --> 00:13:47,080
So, we'll need to make

160
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:49,880
250,000 a month.

161
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:52,080
Geez. Two hundred and fifty thousand?

162
00:13:52,160 --> 00:13:54,080
Are you sure we can do it?

163
00:13:54,880 --> 00:13:57,720
Of course, Mom.
I've already planned everything.

164
00:13:57,800 --> 00:14:01,080
Our guaranteed income
will come from Phetkla's semen,

165
00:14:01,160 --> 00:14:03,360
-product reviews, and TikTok videos.
-Right.

166
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:06,320
We're also selling hydroponic greens,
Pangola grass, and mushrooms.

167
00:14:07,920 --> 00:14:09,320
But…

168
00:14:11,680 --> 00:14:13,520
I actually want you
to sell meatballs again.

169
00:14:14,480 --> 00:14:15,400
Please?

170
00:14:15,480 --> 00:14:17,080
Please?

171
00:14:17,880 --> 00:14:19,200
Mm.

172
00:14:19,280 --> 00:14:20,960
I actually thought about that too.

173
00:14:21,040 --> 00:14:25,480
I was at the market
outside your store the other day.

174
00:14:25,560 --> 00:14:28,080
It was packed!

175
00:14:28,160 --> 00:14:30,280
I think I'll go book a stall there.

176
00:14:31,280 --> 00:14:32,480
That's good.

177
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:36,000
I'll sign you up
for a food delivery app then.

178
00:14:36,080 --> 00:14:38,840
So you can take online orders
while selling at the market.

179
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:40,400
You'll make money both ways.

180
00:14:40,480 --> 00:14:41,880
-Okay.
-Okay?

181
00:14:41,960 --> 00:14:43,200
Good job.

182
00:14:44,280 --> 00:14:47,240
Auem, I had a look at your TikTok account.

183
00:14:47,320 --> 00:14:50,360
It feels a little bit
too academic sometimes.

184
00:14:51,080 --> 00:14:52,760
How about we try jumping on the trend?

185
00:14:53,720 --> 00:14:55,600
-Jump on the trend? How?
-Yeah.

186
00:14:55,680 --> 00:14:56,520
How, dear?

187
00:15:00,520 --> 00:15:01,520
Right, look at this.

188
00:15:11,520 --> 00:15:14,160
Whatever song's trending,
we'll dance to it with the buffaloes.

189
00:15:14,240 --> 00:15:15,400
With the buffaloes?

190
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:19,360
Yeah, so we go viral.
And then we'll get more viewers.

191
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:22,080
-Then we can sell more products.
-How clever!

192
00:15:22,680 --> 00:15:25,120
Wouldn't we just be copying them though?

193
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:27,560
But there's no harm in trying.

194
00:15:27,640 --> 00:15:31,120
Orn's more active on social media
and knows more people online than we do.

195
00:15:31,200 --> 00:15:33,000
This might actually work.

196
00:15:33,760 --> 00:15:35,800
I'll come up with some ideas for you.

197
00:15:35,880 --> 00:15:36,840
Then after school,

198
00:15:36,920 --> 00:15:38,920
I'll help you and Ob
with the livestream sales.

199
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:41,720
Alright, let's join forces.

200
00:15:41,800 --> 00:15:42,840
What?

201
00:15:43,600 --> 00:15:46,080
We're joining forces, of course.
Give me your hand.

202
00:15:46,160 --> 00:15:47,480
Yes, I'm in.

203
00:15:47,560 --> 00:15:48,600
Oh, like this?

204
00:15:48,680 --> 00:15:51,360
-Here.
-Yes. Now say "we can do this" together.

205
00:15:51,440 --> 00:15:53,200
One, two, three…

206
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:55,160
We can do it!

207
00:15:57,880 --> 00:15:59,440
Let me help.

208
00:15:59,520 --> 00:16:02,240
-Help who?
-Help Auem, of course.

209
00:16:02,320 --> 00:16:03,400
Alright.

210
00:16:03,480 --> 00:16:06,120
-That's more like it.
-Well, of course.

211
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:07,920
I have to help Auem somehow.

212
00:16:09,320 --> 00:16:10,840
We have to get Hom Thong back.

213
00:16:10,920 --> 00:16:12,080
DO IT FOR HOM THONG

214
00:16:31,160 --> 00:16:34,400
BEAUTY QUEEN SA-ING'S MEATBALLS

215
00:16:42,480 --> 00:16:45,720
-Only 150 baht!
-For 150, you get a small bag,

216
00:16:45,800 --> 00:16:49,280
but for 300, you can get a big bag.
It's totally worth it.

217
00:16:49,360 --> 00:16:51,480
That's the same amount
as three small packs!

218
00:16:51,560 --> 00:16:53,760
YOGURT, PANGOLA, ORGANIC, SHAMPOO

219
00:17:08,319 --> 00:17:11,480
ANIMAL FEED FOR SALE

220
00:17:11,560 --> 00:17:13,920
Din, Orn, come get some vitamin drinks.

221
00:17:15,960 --> 00:17:17,520
This one's for you, Din.

222
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:32,320
-Thank you very much.
-Thank you.

223
00:17:35,920 --> 00:17:38,640
Here they are.
And here are the other three recipes.

224
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:39,920
Here, look.

225
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:42,920
The one with the white cap
is our original recipe.

226
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:45,920
And this one with the orange cap
is the Northeastern recipe

227
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:47,360
with a Western twist.

228
00:17:47,440 --> 00:17:49,040
But wait, there's more.

229
00:17:49,120 --> 00:17:52,280
For extra umami, go for the red cap.

230
00:17:52,360 --> 00:17:55,000
I can tell you,
they're all absolutely delicious.

231
00:17:57,360 --> 00:17:58,320
Wow!

232
00:17:58,960 --> 00:18:00,360
It's super tasty!

233
00:18:01,120 --> 00:18:03,200
Alright, say ah…

234
00:18:03,280 --> 00:18:04,120
MAE RIEN FERMENTED FISH SAUCE

235
00:18:04,200 --> 00:18:05,520
Good?

236
00:18:06,040 --> 00:18:07,400
Wow, I love the umami.

237
00:18:09,720 --> 00:18:11,720
Go on, eat up.

238
00:18:13,120 --> 00:18:14,440
Good boy.

239
00:18:14,520 --> 00:18:15,800
-Din!
-Hmm?

240
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:20,200
My family and I
managed to make 207,000 this month!

241
00:18:21,160 --> 00:18:23,680
Hang on. 207,000?

242
00:18:23,760 --> 00:18:26,720
-Yeah.
-Wow, congrats!

243
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:30,800
So you're not too stressed out
about your family now?

244
00:18:35,600 --> 00:18:38,000
Oh, Din. How do we know

245
00:18:38,080 --> 00:18:40,640
when Hom Ngern and Phetkla
are ready to mate?

246
00:18:41,240 --> 00:18:43,160
Actually, when a female is in heat,

247
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:46,160
a male will know,
and they'll mate naturally.

248
00:18:47,480 --> 00:18:49,920
You'll have to keep an eye on Hom Ngern.

249
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:52,960
Once she's in heat,
just let Phetkla into her pen.

250
00:18:58,240 --> 00:18:59,920
MR. CHETTHA

251
00:19:03,280 --> 00:19:04,800
Hello, Mr. Chettha.

252
00:19:07,640 --> 00:19:09,120
What products?

253
00:19:09,760 --> 00:19:11,520
I didn't keep any of the products.

254
00:19:11,600 --> 00:19:13,560
I always returned them
after livestreaming.

255
00:19:13,640 --> 00:19:17,560
But the amount you returned
doesn't match what you took out.

256
00:19:21,080 --> 00:19:22,640
Like the pesticides.

257
00:19:22,720 --> 00:19:24,960
You checked out five cases
for the livestream,

258
00:19:25,040 --> 00:19:28,320
but you returned only four.

259
00:19:28,400 --> 00:19:29,680
Where's the fifth case then?

260
00:19:30,400 --> 00:19:34,320
And not just that.
A lot of our stuff has gone missing too.

261
00:19:35,120 --> 00:19:38,320
If you took them,
just come clean right now.

262
00:19:39,120 --> 00:19:40,800
But I didn't!

263
00:19:40,880 --> 00:19:42,640
You can ask Rung.

264
00:19:42,720 --> 00:19:45,160
She was always there with me
when I returned the products.

265
00:19:45,240 --> 00:19:47,040
So you're not going to own up to it?

266
00:20:00,360 --> 00:20:02,320
Oh, Rut? What are you doing here?

267
00:20:04,320 --> 00:20:05,680
Sorry, Auntie.

268
00:20:05,760 --> 00:20:08,480
I'm here to look for stuff
that Auem stole from the store.

269
00:20:08,560 --> 00:20:10,600
What? Stole?

270
00:20:11,600 --> 00:20:12,760
What did she steal?

271
00:20:18,040 --> 00:20:19,840
-Ko, go look inside.
-Got it.

272
00:20:19,920 --> 00:20:22,440
-You guys, look around here.
-Hey, what are you doing?

273
00:20:22,520 --> 00:20:24,360
Hey!

274
00:20:25,800 --> 00:20:26,880
What's going on?

275
00:20:26,960 --> 00:20:28,200
Look.

276
00:20:28,280 --> 00:20:30,480
Auem's not a thief. You must be mistaken.

277
00:20:31,080 --> 00:20:32,760
We'll find out about that.

278
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:36,080
What's happening?

279
00:20:37,840 --> 00:20:38,800
Move.

280
00:20:39,640 --> 00:20:40,480
Stay out of this.

281
00:20:47,200 --> 00:20:49,200
Hey. Hey!

282
00:20:50,160 --> 00:20:51,040
Hang on.

283
00:20:52,320 --> 00:20:53,240
Hey!

284
00:20:57,440 --> 00:20:58,600
-Hey.
-Hey!

285
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:01,200
Why don't you tell me

286
00:21:01,280 --> 00:21:03,400
what Auem stole from the store? Huh?

287
00:21:04,520 --> 00:21:06,520
The stuff she's been selling
on livestream.

288
00:21:06,600 --> 00:21:10,440
Things have gone missing
since Auem started livestreaming.

289
00:21:10,520 --> 00:21:12,000
If not her, then who else?

290
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:29,840
CHETTHA

291
00:21:59,840 --> 00:22:01,560
The evidence is right here.

292
00:22:02,280 --> 00:22:04,440
Are you still gonna deny it?

293
00:22:06,040 --> 00:22:07,480
But I really didn't do anything.

294
00:22:08,440 --> 00:22:09,800
Stop denying it.

295
00:22:09,880 --> 00:22:12,920
If you didn't steal them,
why are they at your house?

296
00:22:13,000 --> 00:22:14,480
Someone must've planted them there.

297
00:22:18,200 --> 00:22:19,800
And I know exactly

298
00:22:19,880 --> 00:22:21,000
who did it.

299
00:22:31,200 --> 00:22:32,520
What was that?

300
00:23:29,680 --> 00:23:31,960
CHETTHA KASET FARM

301
00:23:48,880 --> 00:23:52,320
Ob and I saw someone in here last night.

302
00:23:52,400 --> 00:23:55,560
When we checked the storage room,
these things were already there.

303
00:23:55,640 --> 00:23:58,800
But why would they hide these at yours?

304
00:23:58,880 --> 00:24:00,840
Someone must've told them to.

305
00:24:01,560 --> 00:24:02,760
Ming and Rut?

306
00:24:03,400 --> 00:24:04,400
Yes.

307
00:24:04,480 --> 00:24:07,240
Those two probably want to see me fired.

308
00:24:07,320 --> 00:24:10,600
I knew something was off
the moment they suggested I livestream.

309
00:24:10,680 --> 00:24:12,440
It was so unlike them.

310
00:24:13,040 --> 00:24:14,840
Should we tell Mr. Chettha?

311
00:24:15,600 --> 00:24:16,600
Not yet.

312
00:24:17,120 --> 00:24:18,480
I have a better idea.

313
00:24:18,560 --> 00:24:20,200
Alright, I'm going to leave this here.

314
00:24:22,680 --> 00:24:23,600
Hom Ngern.

315
00:24:24,640 --> 00:24:27,920
If a stranger comes into our house,
get them on camera.

316
00:24:58,440 --> 00:24:59,520
Here.

317
00:25:11,800 --> 00:25:13,120
Go get Jak.

318
00:25:13,200 --> 00:25:15,200
I already asked Rung to get him.

319
00:25:15,280 --> 00:25:16,880
He's waiting outside.

320
00:25:18,480 --> 00:25:19,720
Excuse me.

321
00:25:23,200 --> 00:25:25,240
Rung, you can send Jak in now.

322
00:25:32,920 --> 00:25:36,120
Why did you steal my stuff
and pin it on Auem?

323
00:25:37,880 --> 00:25:39,160
Tell me!

324
00:25:41,040 --> 00:25:42,840
I don't think Jak will talk.

325
00:25:43,600 --> 00:25:46,920
I guess
we can let the footage speak for itself

326
00:25:47,000 --> 00:25:49,000
and save everyone's time. Here.

327
00:25:50,040 --> 00:25:53,360
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">I snuck the goods over to Auem's</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">just like you told me to, Ms. Ming.</font></font></i>

328
00:25:58,480 --> 00:26:00,960
When I finally get Auem fired,

329
00:26:01,040 --> 00:26:02,600
I'll promote you myself.

330
00:26:03,240 --> 00:26:04,200
Thank you.

331
00:26:14,840 --> 00:26:18,200
-I can explain, Dad.
-Go wait outside.

332
00:26:18,280 --> 00:26:19,360
And get Rut in here!

333
00:26:20,080 --> 00:26:21,040
Go!

334
00:26:30,720 --> 00:26:33,920
Karma sure bites back
pretty fast these days, Ms. Ming.

335
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:44,160
How's it going, Ming? Has Auem been fired?

336
00:26:45,200 --> 00:26:47,680
Someone's definitely fired.
Not Auem though.

337
00:26:48,520 --> 00:26:52,080
But some people around here.

338
00:26:54,240 --> 00:26:55,160
Let's go.

339
00:27:01,200 --> 00:27:02,640
I'm sorry I misjudged you.

340
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:07,200
And I'm sorry
that my daughter did you wrong.

341
00:27:07,800 --> 00:27:09,640
But I've got to ask you a favor.

342
00:27:09,720 --> 00:27:10,760
Don't press charges.

343
00:27:10,840 --> 00:27:12,880
I'll punish Ming myself.

344
00:27:12,960 --> 00:27:15,000
Rut and Jak will get it too.

345
00:27:16,480 --> 00:27:17,680
Okay.

346
00:27:17,760 --> 00:27:21,200
But I've got something for you.

347
00:27:22,480 --> 00:27:23,880
Here.

348
00:27:28,640 --> 00:27:30,120
I'd like to resign.

349
00:27:30,200 --> 00:27:31,160
SEPTEMBER 30, 2025

350
00:27:31,240 --> 00:27:33,080
LETTER OF RESIGNATION
FROM CHETTHA KASET FARM

351
00:27:33,160 --> 00:27:35,320
I don't want to let
a great employee like you go.

352
00:27:36,080 --> 00:27:37,120
How about this?

353
00:27:38,120 --> 00:27:39,200
I'll give you a raise.

354
00:27:40,280 --> 00:27:41,360
Thank you.

355
00:27:42,040 --> 00:27:43,800
But as long as I'm here,

356
00:27:43,880 --> 00:27:45,520
Ms. Ming won't stop.

357
00:27:45,600 --> 00:27:48,360
And it'll only put you
in an awkward position.

358
00:27:51,800 --> 00:27:55,280
But please don't worry.
I may have quit this job,

359
00:27:55,360 --> 00:27:58,400
but you can still hire me
for product reviews.

360
00:27:58,480 --> 00:27:59,880
I now work on a job-by-job basis.

361
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:08,440
It was so damn satisfying
to see the look on Rut's face

362
00:28:08,520 --> 00:28:10,840
when he got demoted
and his salary got cut.

363
00:28:13,800 --> 00:28:16,000
But you did think it through, right?

364
00:28:16,080 --> 00:28:17,280
About quitting.

365
00:28:17,360 --> 00:28:20,440
I did. I don't want any more trouble,

366
00:28:20,520 --> 00:28:22,240
and I'm tired of fighting with Ming.

367
00:28:22,320 --> 00:28:23,240
Besides,

368
00:28:23,320 --> 00:28:26,200
now I can go all out on my buffalo farm.

369
00:28:26,280 --> 00:28:27,120
Right?

370
00:28:29,960 --> 00:28:31,880
You think you're so high and mighty?

371
00:28:31,960 --> 00:28:34,520
Think you're so cool
for quitting the job yourself?

372
00:28:35,120 --> 00:28:38,000
She already quit.
What more do you want from her?

373
00:28:38,080 --> 00:28:39,520
Let's see how far you get

374
00:28:39,600 --> 00:28:43,160
because I'll never let my dad
have you back.

375
00:28:44,160 --> 00:28:45,720
You don't need to worry about that.

376
00:28:45,800 --> 00:28:48,480
I wouldn't come back here
in a million years.

377
00:28:48,560 --> 00:28:49,960
I'd hate to see you lose again.

378
00:28:51,560 --> 00:28:53,280
Don't get so cocky, Auem.

379
00:28:53,880 --> 00:28:55,360
Your family's got nothing but debt.

380
00:28:55,440 --> 00:28:58,960
And your buffalo conservation center?
It's nothing but a fantasy.

381
00:28:59,040 --> 00:29:01,000
You'll never get anywhere.

382
00:29:01,080 --> 00:29:02,800
Well, just wait and see.

383
00:29:02,880 --> 00:29:06,160
Whatever happens, I know I'll go further
than you and Ming ever will.

384
00:29:08,400 --> 00:29:09,720
Let's go, Rung.

385
00:29:10,480 --> 00:29:11,880
Just you wait!

386
00:29:13,120 --> 00:29:14,520
Go back to your buffaloes!

387
00:29:17,040 --> 00:29:20,360
If you're a party animal
or a karaoke lover,

388
00:29:20,440 --> 00:29:24,200
check out this set. It comes with
a mic, speaker, and light effects!

389
00:29:25,200 --> 00:29:27,920
Phetkla, let's make some noise.

390
00:29:30,080 --> 00:29:33,600
Auem! How could you quit your job
just like that? Huh?

391
00:29:36,920 --> 00:29:40,800
Aunt Sa-Ang told me everything.
Rut came to get stuff from ours

392
00:29:40,880 --> 00:29:44,160
to get you in trouble, didn't he?
You should've told me! I'd kick his butt.

393
00:29:44,240 --> 00:29:45,480
It's okay, Mom.

394
00:29:45,560 --> 00:29:48,400
Breaking up with Rut already freed me
from bad karma with him.

395
00:29:50,320 --> 00:29:53,680
I guess you're right.
Good thing he never became my son-in-law.

396
00:29:53,760 --> 00:29:54,760
Exactly, Auntie.

397
00:29:55,560 --> 00:29:58,680
You're better off
with a new son-in-law candidate.

398
00:29:58,760 --> 00:30:02,360
There's a really nice son-in-law
around here, you know?

399
00:30:02,440 --> 00:30:04,320
Right, Phetkla?

400
00:30:08,560 --> 00:30:09,760
Oh, Auem.

401
00:30:09,840 --> 00:30:10,680
Yeah?

402
00:30:10,760 --> 00:30:12,160
Now that you've quit your job,

403
00:30:12,240 --> 00:30:14,280
our monthly income is down by half.

404
00:30:14,360 --> 00:30:17,760
Mom, don't worry.
I already did some calculations.

405
00:30:17,840 --> 00:30:21,240
We actually make more from the farm
than from my job.

406
00:30:21,320 --> 00:30:23,800
So I just want to go all in with the farm.

407
00:30:23,880 --> 00:30:25,600
Maybe we'll make even more money.

408
00:30:26,560 --> 00:30:28,160
And what if we don't?

409
00:30:29,240 --> 00:30:30,560
Why wouldn't we?

410
00:30:30,640 --> 00:30:33,160
Auem's got all of us here to help her.

411
00:30:35,200 --> 00:30:36,320
Mom.

412
00:30:37,240 --> 00:30:38,800
Trust me.

413
00:30:38,880 --> 00:30:41,920
I promise that I'll make it happen.

414
00:30:43,840 --> 00:30:44,960
Okay.

415
00:30:55,800 --> 00:30:57,000
-Din.
-Hmm?

416
00:30:57,080 --> 00:30:58,640
Other than buffalo dung,

417
00:30:58,720 --> 00:31:02,120
is there anything else from buffaloes
that we can put to good use?

418
00:31:02,840 --> 00:31:04,520
Well, there's buffalo milk.

419
00:31:05,160 --> 00:31:06,720
But we have only two females here.

420
00:31:06,800 --> 00:31:08,080
We don't have enough milk.

421
00:31:10,320 --> 00:31:11,360
Right, come on in.

422
00:31:11,440 --> 00:31:12,880
Just put them right here.

423
00:31:14,480 --> 00:31:15,960
Yeah, right here.

424
00:31:16,040 --> 00:31:18,040
-Go on.
-What's this, Dad?

425
00:31:18,120 --> 00:31:21,320
Buffalo milk. The locals
couldn't sell all of it,

426
00:31:21,400 --> 00:31:24,440
so they want us to help sell their milk.

427
00:31:31,920 --> 00:31:34,760
-Please, have a look.
-Well, what can we do

428
00:31:34,840 --> 00:31:36,120
with buffalo milk?

429
00:31:36,200 --> 00:31:38,520
A lot, actually.

430
00:31:38,600 --> 00:31:42,360
Some people use it in cooking.
Last time, your aunt made

431
00:31:42,440 --> 00:31:45,280
a spicy curry with some buffalo milk.

432
00:31:45,360 --> 00:31:47,080
It was out of this world.

433
00:31:48,240 --> 00:31:50,920
What else can we do with the milk
other than cooking?

434
00:31:51,680 --> 00:31:52,760
Ob!

435
00:31:53,280 --> 00:31:56,480
-You stole my yogurt again!
-What's going on? Easy!

436
00:31:56,560 --> 00:31:57,400
-Hey!
-Ob!

437
00:31:57,480 --> 00:32:00,160
-Come on, I only took one. Go get more!
-You stole it again!

438
00:32:00,240 --> 00:32:01,640
-You go get more!
-Ob!

439
00:32:02,240 --> 00:32:04,600
-Stop it, Ob! Orn, you too!
-Ob!

440
00:32:04,680 --> 00:32:05,840
Ugh, I'm out of breath!

441
00:32:05,920 --> 00:32:07,880
Why fight over a tub of yogurt?

442
00:32:07,960 --> 00:32:11,320
-Give me that!
-Just one! Orn, just go buy some more.

443
00:32:11,400 --> 00:32:14,120
-You go!
-It's the last one! You go!

444
00:32:14,880 --> 00:32:16,000
I know!

445
00:32:17,400 --> 00:32:19,280
I'll make yogurt from buffalo milk.

446
00:32:19,360 --> 00:32:21,160
It'll be our farm's new product.

447
00:32:21,760 --> 00:32:23,240
Buffalo milk yogurt?

448
00:32:25,280 --> 00:32:26,520
Buffalo milk?

449
00:32:26,600 --> 00:32:27,480
Yeah.

450
00:32:28,760 --> 00:32:29,640
Dad.

451
00:32:30,160 --> 00:32:33,560
I'm learning how to make yogurt today
with Uncle Tik's friend.

452
00:32:33,640 --> 00:32:35,520
If I can make this work,

453
00:32:35,600 --> 00:32:38,120
I'll buy buffalo milk from the locals.

454
00:32:38,200 --> 00:32:39,840
They'll have more income that way.

455
00:32:40,440 --> 00:32:44,680
And I'll sell this buffalo milk yogurt
at our buffalo conservation center.

456
00:32:46,240 --> 00:32:48,320
Please wish me luck.

457
00:32:48,400 --> 00:32:50,680
BOONYOD THADAMIT

458
00:32:53,400 --> 00:32:56,960
SORNSIRI THAI BUFFALO FARM

459
00:32:57,040 --> 00:32:59,920
KAEW FA THE BREEDING BULL

460
00:33:08,720 --> 00:33:09,960
-Here they are.
-Oh.

461
00:33:11,480 --> 00:33:13,400
-Hello.
-Hello.

462
00:33:13,480 --> 00:33:15,680
This is Tom. He's my junior and a friend.

463
00:33:15,760 --> 00:33:17,040
He's a teacher here.

464
00:33:17,640 --> 00:33:19,120
This is Auem.

465
00:33:20,320 --> 00:33:21,920
And this is Dindaen.

466
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:23,360
He's helping her with the farm.

467
00:33:23,960 --> 00:33:25,040
Yes.

468
00:33:25,120 --> 00:33:27,040
I'm sorry about your father.

469
00:33:27,120 --> 00:33:28,680
Tik already told me.

470
00:33:29,400 --> 00:33:32,000
-I was shocked when I heard.
-You knew my dad?

471
00:33:32,680 --> 00:33:33,640
Of course.

472
00:33:34,160 --> 00:33:37,160
Tom used to consult Yod
about his research quite often.

473
00:33:37,240 --> 00:33:40,880
He already promised
to teach you two everything he knows

474
00:33:40,960 --> 00:33:42,720
to repay Yod for all the help he gave him.

475
00:33:42,800 --> 00:33:43,640
Of course.

476
00:33:44,840 --> 00:33:46,640
Alright, shall we?

477
00:33:46,720 --> 00:33:48,240
-Sure.
-Let's go.

478
00:33:48,320 --> 00:33:49,480
Let's go.

479
00:33:52,080 --> 00:33:57,040
Most Thai people believe
that buffaloes are for ploughing fields

480
00:33:57,120 --> 00:34:00,720
or for making baby buffaloes,
and then they're just sold off.

481
00:34:01,440 --> 00:34:03,640
But buffalo milk is just like cow's milk.

482
00:34:03,720 --> 00:34:06,040
It's very high in protein and calcium

483
00:34:06,120 --> 00:34:08,199
and also rich in healthy fats.

484
00:34:08,800 --> 00:34:10,120
Oh? If that's the case,

485
00:34:10,199 --> 00:34:12,800
then why is cow's milk more popular?

486
00:34:13,320 --> 00:34:14,840
Well, that's because

487
00:34:14,920 --> 00:34:18,000
dairy cows were raised commercially
before buffaloes were

488
00:34:18,080 --> 00:34:19,400
by over a decade.

489
00:34:19,480 --> 00:34:23,080
So instead of buffaloes,
farmers started raising dairy cows.

490
00:34:23,159 --> 00:34:24,639
And most importantly,

491
00:34:24,719 --> 00:34:28,320
a dairy cow can produce
around 15 to 30 liters of milk a day,

492
00:34:28,400 --> 00:34:31,199
but buffaloes produce a lot less.
Only two to five liters a day.

493
00:34:31,920 --> 00:34:33,920
Oh, some people say that

494
00:34:34,000 --> 00:34:36,920
buffalo milk is similar to coconut milk.

495
00:34:37,000 --> 00:34:38,400
What does that mean?

496
00:34:38,480 --> 00:34:39,360
Buffalo milk

497
00:34:39,440 --> 00:34:42,360
is rich, creamy, and full of flavor,
just like coconut milk.

498
00:34:42,960 --> 00:34:46,400
Local people sometimes cook
with buffalo milk

499
00:34:46,480 --> 00:34:48,679
and use it in drinks
instead of cow's milk.

500
00:34:49,400 --> 00:34:51,639
Most importantly, most people don't know

501
00:34:51,719 --> 00:34:54,639
that buffalo milk is very low in lactose.

502
00:34:54,719 --> 00:34:56,840
So those with lactose intolerance
can enjoy it.

503
00:35:00,120 --> 00:35:03,080
Ready to see how buffaloes are milked?

504
00:35:03,160 --> 00:35:03,800
-Yes.
-Yes.

505
00:35:03,880 --> 00:35:05,040
Okay, let's go.

506
00:35:05,120 --> 00:35:06,040
MILKING PARLOR

507
00:35:06,120 --> 00:35:07,480
DISINFECTANT FOOTBATH

508
00:35:22,000 --> 00:35:25,760
As you can see here,
before we can milk the buffaloes,

509
00:35:25,840 --> 00:35:28,320
we need to move them
into a sanitized area.

510
00:35:29,120 --> 00:35:30,400
Then we clean their udder.

511
00:35:30,480 --> 00:35:33,200
We use a cloth soaked in warm water

512
00:35:33,280 --> 00:35:35,320
to wipe down the whole udder.

513
00:35:36,280 --> 00:35:39,440
You also need to massage the udder
while wiping it.

514
00:35:39,520 --> 00:35:43,000
This is because
there are milk ducts in the udder.

515
00:35:43,600 --> 00:35:45,800
They're connected to the milk glands.

516
00:35:45,880 --> 00:35:47,920
We'll have to open those up.

517
00:35:48,000 --> 00:35:50,600
Once that's done,
we'll need the black tray.

518
00:35:50,680 --> 00:35:52,080
See? He just got one.

519
00:35:52,160 --> 00:35:55,640
Then he'll express a little milk
from each teat to check it.

520
00:35:55,720 --> 00:35:58,560
If the milk comes out
its normal white color, it's fine.

521
00:35:58,640 --> 00:36:02,480
But if it's cloudy and thick like pus,

522
00:36:03,720 --> 00:36:05,480
then there's an infection.

523
00:36:05,560 --> 00:36:07,000
We can't use that milk.

524
00:36:07,080 --> 00:36:08,160
And we must get the buffalo
treated right away

525
00:36:09,280 --> 00:36:11,680
since it's contagious.

526
00:36:11,760 --> 00:36:15,360
Got it? If even one part is infected,
we can't use any of the milk.

527
00:36:32,080 --> 00:36:36,000
After milking and storing the milk
in chilled containers,

528
00:36:36,080 --> 00:36:37,400
next is pasteurization,

529
00:36:38,080 --> 00:36:39,200
or sterilization.

530
00:36:51,480 --> 00:36:54,000
Okay, we're going to measure
the milk temperature first.

531
00:36:54,080 --> 00:36:56,520
It should be
at a relatively low temperature.

532
00:36:56,600 --> 00:36:57,760
If it's too hot,

533
00:36:57,840 --> 00:37:00,360
the starter culture we add
won't ferment properly.

534
00:37:09,720 --> 00:37:12,400
You can pour it into containers
and let it set.

535
00:37:12,480 --> 00:37:14,600
Then we heat it again.

536
00:37:24,800 --> 00:37:27,640
YOGURT

537
00:37:30,920 --> 00:37:32,280
It's nice and rainy today.

538
00:37:32,360 --> 00:37:35,520
I've got some yogurt I learned to make
for you all to taste.

539
00:37:35,600 --> 00:37:37,800
Well, give it a try and tell me

540
00:37:37,880 --> 00:37:39,360
if you think it's got potential.

541
00:37:39,440 --> 00:37:40,800
Wow.

542
00:37:47,160 --> 00:37:49,280
Aren't you going to try it?

543
00:37:49,960 --> 00:37:51,320
I don't know how to eat this.

544
00:37:51,400 --> 00:37:53,200
It smells kinda off.

545
00:37:53,280 --> 00:37:54,760
Milk is enough for me.

546
00:37:56,080 --> 00:37:59,120
Both milk and yogurt are good for you.

547
00:37:59,200 --> 00:38:02,720
But yogurt is better for your intestines
and bowel movements

548
00:38:02,800 --> 00:38:04,960
since it has good bacteria.

549
00:38:05,040 --> 00:38:07,400
A perfect fix for constipation
and poor digestion.

550
00:38:08,000 --> 00:38:10,280
Open your mouth. Open it.

551
00:38:13,920 --> 00:38:16,040
-How is it?
-Look at your face.

552
00:38:18,480 --> 00:38:19,320
It's good.

553
00:38:21,120 --> 00:38:22,720
Not bad at all.

554
00:38:22,800 --> 00:38:25,200
-Get a nice spoonful!
-Not bad at all.

555
00:38:25,960 --> 00:38:27,200
This is so good, Auem.

556
00:38:27,280 --> 00:38:29,920
I thought it'd smell stronger
and be harder to stomach.

557
00:38:30,760 --> 00:38:31,960
It's delicious.

558
00:38:32,040 --> 00:38:35,480
The tartness is just right.
You should sell it just like this.

559
00:38:36,080 --> 00:38:37,560
But personally, I think

560
00:38:37,640 --> 00:38:38,920
it could be a little sweeter.

561
00:38:39,000 --> 00:38:41,720
Why? This flavor is perfect
for health-conscious people.

562
00:38:41,800 --> 00:38:43,920
They don't like sweet stuff.

563
00:38:44,000 --> 00:38:45,600
But I do.

564
00:38:45,680 --> 00:38:48,440
No one else does, though. Just you.

565
00:38:49,000 --> 00:38:50,200
-Now, now.
-Just eat it.

566
00:38:50,280 --> 00:38:52,640
-See?
-Alright, alright. No arguing.

567
00:38:52,720 --> 00:38:53,560
Here you go.

568
00:38:53,640 --> 00:38:56,560
-This will balance out the tartness.
-Whoa.

569
00:38:56,640 --> 00:39:00,160
If you're a sweet tooth,
add some fruit to your yogurt.

570
00:39:12,560 --> 00:39:15,680
-Try it.
-Look, it's straw-buried.

571
00:39:15,760 --> 00:39:17,800
-Strawberries!
-Strawberries!

572
00:39:18,400 --> 00:39:19,240
Come on.

573
00:39:19,320 --> 00:39:23,440
It's really great with some raisins.
Nice and chewy.

574
00:39:24,040 --> 00:39:25,320
It's good, sis.

575
00:39:25,400 --> 00:39:28,760
Will you sell the yogurt with fruit?

576
00:39:29,520 --> 00:39:32,720
Yes. I'll make small fruit cups

577
00:39:32,800 --> 00:39:35,320
and sell them with the yogurt,
giving customers more options.

578
00:39:35,400 --> 00:39:36,720
Clever girl.

579
00:39:36,800 --> 00:39:39,600
That's a good idea.
We can use seasonal fruit.

580
00:39:39,680 --> 00:39:41,000
Keep the customers entertained.

581
00:39:41,080 --> 00:39:43,520
Some of the villagers grow fruit,

582
00:39:43,600 --> 00:39:45,520
so I asked them to sell us some.

583
00:39:45,600 --> 00:39:47,600
They'll earn some money that way too.

584
00:39:47,680 --> 00:39:49,440
-Good idea.
-Yeah.

585
00:39:50,200 --> 00:39:52,000
BOONYOD FARM

586
00:39:56,680 --> 00:39:58,560
Hey, Hom Ngern.

587
00:39:59,120 --> 00:40:01,040
Everyone in our family

588
00:40:01,120 --> 00:40:04,200
is working hard to earn enough money
to buy your baby back.

589
00:40:04,720 --> 00:40:06,320
Aren't you happy?

590
00:40:10,760 --> 00:40:13,560
But I am. I so am.

591
00:40:14,200 --> 00:40:15,880
I'm happy everyone's helping out.

592
00:40:18,080 --> 00:40:20,800
Tomorrow, I'll bring some yogurt

593
00:40:20,880 --> 00:40:23,840
to sell at Mom's meatballs shop
and Auntie's shop at school.

594
00:40:24,480 --> 00:40:26,920
If this sells well, I'm sure that

595
00:40:27,000 --> 00:40:30,520
we can make five grand
in the next three months.

596
00:40:31,440 --> 00:40:33,160
Just hang in there.

597
00:42:14,280 --> 00:42:15,200
Subtitle translation by:
Narawan Promprakai
